<title>ANGOLA: PRESS DIGEST - Angola - May 19.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - Angola - May 19.</headline>
<dateline>LUANDA 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the leading stories in the Angolan press on Monday.</p>
<p>Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- - - -</p>
<p>CORREIO DA SEMANA</p>
<p>- UNITA deputy and spokesman for the party, Jaka Jamba, has blasted the government in an open letter for failing to pay striking teachers' salaries owed since January.</p>
<p>- The newspaper said in an editorial that South African-based De Beers is to build a diamond sorting office in Luanda.</p>
<p>--Luanda newsroom +2442 360-849</p>
